  "established": [
    "Landscape flag bit0 builds the clipped horizon, while bit1 gates the separately generated ground grid. P toggles bit1; reset sets both. The original entry and state conditions remain.",
    "The selected world colour supplies the lower fill and queued horizon polygon. The upper fill uses 15 in Amiga/alternate mode0, while alternate mode1 explicitly retains zero. Split row separates upper/lower fills.",
    "The adjacent maxY word is a writer snapshot with no recovered direct reader. It is not asserted dead or used as the lower-fill end; the consumers use current viewport maxY.",
    "The debug flag gates resource refresh, extra commands and viewer diagnostics. It is not a universal invulnerability guarantee.",
    "The face-visibility flag bypasses cached/backface rejection, while ordinary projection and screen clipping still apply. Viewer input waiting and world-object update gates are named for their observed readers; unsupported incoming writers remain unknown.",
    "The world-transition byte snapshots space/surface state at procedure entry, then detects changes after world/surface decisions. It is not assumed to be a previous physical-frame value."
  ],
